    "knowledge_point": "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula",
    "problem": "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}).$",
    "worked_solution": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=4$ and $r=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{4}{2}) & =\\frac{4!}{(4-2)!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2!}{2!\\cdot 2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
